agraph","page":11,"text":"CLAIM: People should be encouraged to travel by bicycle rather than by car.","bbox":[108.0199966430664,528.59033203125,522.2727661132812,541.4739990234375]},"ce0b2e88b5d637bace3f":{"type":"paragraph","page":11,"text":"ARGUMENT: Maintaining a bicycle is less expensive than a car.","bbox":[108.0199966430664,559.580322265625,455.43280029296875,572.4639892578125]},"5130f7e86b9d1c2eb52f":{"type":"paragraph","page":11,"text":"EVIDENCE: 1. The parts of a bicycle are much cheaper than the parts","bbox":[108.0199966430664,590.5403442382812,493.2328186035156,603.4240112304688]},"adb868db8ef77fee76d2":{"type":"paragraph","page":11,"text":"of a car.","bbox":[72.02400207519531,606.1403198242188,193.06280517578125,619.0239868164062]},"e8c8e9b945060628f1bb":{"type":"paragraph","page":11,"text":"2. Fixing a car may require the services of a mechanic who would charge an expensive amount for labor. On the other hand, many bicycles can be fixed by the owners themselves. 3. Cars require expensive yearly registration.","bbox":[108.0199966430664,621.620361328125,526.5465698242188,680.9439697265625]},"899aedb247cf2423321f":{"type":"paragraph","page":11,"text":"COUNTERARGUMENT: Some say that riding a bicycle would increase","bbox":[108.0199966430664,699.0203247070312,489.1528015136719,711.9039916992188]},"d4549f1a0684b31a5782":{"type":"paragraph","page":11,"text":"travel time and decrease productivity.","bbox":[216.0500030517578,714.5203247070312,425.8828125,727.4039916992188]},"9dd6c3eb300310238567":{"type":"paragraph","page":12,"text":"REBUTTAL: Traveling by bicycle would actually mean avoiding rush hour","bbox":[108.0199966430664,71.9402847290039,519.3927612304688,84.82396697998047]},"606b2a6915385ac941df":{"type":"paragraph","page":12,"text":"Traffic jams.","bbox":[72.02400207519531,87.42032623291016,248.02281188964844,100.30400848388672]},"a9b35008b5b1b0e1932e":{"type":"paragraph","page":12,"text":"CONCLUSION: So, we encourage people to travel by bicycle rather than by car","bbox":[108.0199966430664,118.38028717041016,526.7548217773438,131.2639617919922]},"8cb8ab6a62ed6ed760ac":{"type":"paragraph","page":12,"text":"to avoid traffic jams during rush hours to keep and it does not make people from being late to their appointments.","bbox":[72.02400207519531,133.86033630371094,526.4637451171875,162.34397888183594]},"7a1556913c9905e0b39a":{"type":"paragraph","page":12,"text":"NOTE: Evidence can be FACTS, STATISTICS, and EXAMPLES","bbox":[72.02400207519531,180.4203338623047,420.5835876464844,193.3040008544922]},"17bbabb142c3cc2eb55b":{"type":"paragraph","page":12,"text":"After knowing the elements of an argumentative essay, we also need to learn","bbox":[108.0199966430664,211.3802947998047,522.9725952148438,224.2639617919922]},"a8cb2cd0115a5a019b60":{"type":"paragraph","page":12,"text":"the components of an argumentative essay.","bbox":[72.02400207519531,226.8903045654297,322.20281982421875,239.7739715576172]}},"excerptBlocks":{"concepts:0":["0337ea8b7df6e470723b","aff4bf2fb31bc39157fd","4cf82c39afc566f59b3d","b35e3a8acda6f2b34e23","39c251e022fe087375ea","a5ca0d4a105875d11f81","6ba8ff39d31b8461da0b","d746593b8901236344a2","4f113cf3f906283278f4","c464e5bbf0c9f11fa2ea","b2c5347c51bb3c9034dd","a1891027abda0c3de2c7","41f3e73858cc64d8300a","081d59f4943749164d5e","4b4373460479034c4a1c","4966574d17818fc07372","b8ddd713b9a9e77fb5f9","a039e8251d205f64ea0a","238fcb3b1bf68a94dea1","bcadc70db47f7526b51d","54c3b57d9222dfdeba99","d042162fd0db6c54ea45","ad2c67b61742d0815a9e","6c931078ec6bde7d14be","088c6b820cd67c4258a1","c089015237f030a6ed09","5845f6353826d89625af","4760fa94d8e2b3878fcd","0d7e57031976b12478a2","ce866598f10b2f791326","d7b50b1e8458411208dc","4bf7d3bb6c27675945b6","aeb06bc9b1eefcbecec1","29126d0f27abcc915e72","52216dc52f3e223570a9","7386fbf3f3e039fc3663","b50ebf60b008dd79c7c4","8dbf602321e0dbb5ea8f","7cdde293040543d67dad","7d0ff4e9f61437ae7e3f","681d813260ddbbc65f09","b1d46890da01086dff2c","414911ed3e2ee937ec1f","549f734c880f3